  "summary": "The Mark V is the controller on Tigerflow multi-pump booster packages (up to four VFD pumps). Its BACnet list is monitoring only: every object is read-only. It reports pump run commands and VFD run feedback, HOA positions, pump faults, pressure alarms, suction and system pressure, the pressure setpoint, flow, per-pump speed and run hours.",
  "bacnet_transport": [],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "All 47 objects are printed as Read Only; the BMS cannot start, stop or reset the system over BACnet on the Mark V.",
    "Instances are printed as BV0001.. / AV0001..; the gaps (BV 9-16, 23-32, 41-50, 61) are not in the list.",
    "The point list does not state the BACnet transport (IP or MS/TP) or device addressing.",
    "Units as printed: pressures in psi, flow in GPM, run time in hours."
  ],
